# t-understand

- Treat normal chat questions as the only human entry point.
- Cursor engine path: `~/.cursor/t-understand-engine/agent_runtime.py`.
- Never ask for `ContextRoot`, `$TU`, internal IDs, or pipeline commands.
- On the first substantive repository task, silently bootstrap `.t-understand/` in the active Git worktree and generate all internal identifiers automatically.
- Exclude `.t-understand/**` from source snapshots, discovery, review, and Git operations.
- Load only `tu-*` skills from `@../t-understand/`.
- Allow local read, write, search, shell, build, test, validation, and packaging work without asking for per-action permission.
- Deny outside-workspace access, all `gh` commands, and mutating Git commands. Git is read-only.
- Separate facts, inferences, conflicts, unknowns, and stale knowledge.
- Never apply suggested review patches; hand approved implementation changes to t-think.
- Terminal workers may not delegate.
